# Linear product-spec SOP

Golden template for **linear-product-spec** workflow (`author-product-spec` + `decompose-subgoals`).

## Labels

- Intake gate: `${linear_product_spec_label}` on the Linear issue before webhook fires (or note `needs_spec_present=true` when label present).
- After review, humans add `${linear_implement_label}` to start **linear-spec-implement**.

## Golden template (fill every section)

${golden_product_spec_body}

## Author-product-spec rules

1. Read Linear issue title + description from workflow notes (`linear_issue_title`, `linear_issue_body`).
2. Replace `{TITLE}` with the issue title; preserve marker `<!-- spec-symphony-spec-v1 -->` at top.
3. Expand thin tickets into concrete acceptance criteria (minimum 3 when possible).
4. Note `spec_markdown=` with the full markdown body (single note or chunked with clear delimiter).
5. Do **not** write engineering subgoals in this stage — `decompose-subgoals` owns that section.

## Decompose-subgoals rules

1. read_notes `spec_markdown` from prior stage.
2. Emit 3–8 numbered engineering subgoals (implementation-sized, testable, ordered).
3. Append `## Engineering subgoals` section to spec markdown in notes as `spec_markdown_final=`.
4. Note `engineering_subgoals=` as markdown numbered list only.

## Post-linear-spec-comment

Post `spec_markdown_final` via `${linear_tool_save_comment}` with footer:

```
Reply + add label `${linear_implement_label}` when approved to start implementation.
```
